          <change when="2022-03-08T15:01:59-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready. Followed recommendation of two voters and did not make cosmetic change in line 2. One might argue that, if one underdots the final two letters of Μαρίας, then one might as well underdot ὅτι, because there are faint traces.</change>
          <change when="2022-03-08T12:53:17-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/berkes.lajos">Vote - AcceptText - fine. I agree that the cosmetic change is unnecessary, but there are other views on this in the editorial board. Let the finalizer decide, but if it is kept, it should be marked up as a 'correction' (which should be avoided for such cases in my view).</change>
          <change when="2022-03-08T09:23:03-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">Vote - AcceptText - L. 5 correction looks ok to me. Cosmetic change unnecessary.</change>
          <change when="2022-02-21T10:42:40-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - One significant change in line 5 and a cosmetic one in line 2 (Μαρία̣ς̣). From image.</change>
